WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:04.920
The Cloverfield Paradox has a relatively simple
plot: a space station crew is tasked with

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:09.110
activating a particle accelerator called the
Shepard, which will create a clean and renewable

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:12.009
source of energy for a resource-deprived Earth.

00:00:12.009 --> 00:00:16.320
Things start to get complicated, however,
when the machine creates a rift in space-time,

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.910
propelling the crew into a parallel dimension.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:23.540
Little do they know, this also sets into motion
the events of the first and second Cloverfield

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:24.540
movies.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:30.010
So, how does the movie get from simple a energy
experiment story to an all-out monster invasion

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:31.010
movie?

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:34.800
Let's walk through the last bits of The Cloverfield
Paradox and break it down.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.480
Monster madness

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:40.140
Cloverfield fans have long speculated about
where the monsters from the first movie came

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.810
from, but Paradox finally offers a definitive
answer: they came from another dimension.

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:49.380
Oddly enough, we find this out thanks to an
on-screen interview with a conspiracy theorist,

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:53.470
who warns the world that launching the Shepard
could have devastating consequences.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:57.950
"They risk ripping open the membrane of space-time."

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:01.540
"This experiment could unleash chaos."

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:06.220
His words are unfortunately ignored, of course,
but he's ultimately proven right once an overload

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:10.670
of the Shepard system thrusts the crew into
an alternate reality while introducing untold

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:13.550
numbers of hellbeasts to run roughshod over
Earth.

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:18.440
The film's closing moments reveal that by
2028, there's been a full-on invasion of monsters

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:19.440
all over the planet.

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:22.060
"You're having her come back to these things?"

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:25.750
Judging from the size of the one we do see
pop through the clouds in the last shot, if

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:29.690
there's a significant number of these things
roaming about the place, humans don't stand

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:31.450
a chance.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:33.479
World War What?

00:01:33.479 --> 00:01:37.670
Before the extra-dimensional chaos breaks
out, it's very clear that Earthlings are already

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:40.470
having a lot of trouble sustaining their way
of life.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:44.920
A global energy crisis has put several nations
-- Germany and Russia in particular -- at

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:46.080
the brink of war.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:50.450
And that sense of desperation and paranoia
trickles into the dynamics of the international

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:55.299
space station's crew, which features both
a German and a Russian scientist working on

00:01:55.299 --> 00:01:56.579
different aspects of the mission.

00:01:56.579 --> 00:02:01.230
"I don't have a problem with you" (in Russian)
"but your little German boyfriend here I do."

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:05.220
Once we journey with the crew to the parallel
dimension, we discover that on that Earth,

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:09.590
war has already broken out, and that timeline's
Schmidt actually was a German agent who'd

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:12.450
been sabotaging their mission to stoke the
flames of war.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:17.130
So, chances are, even if the monsters hadn't
shown up, the human race might have gone over

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:18.780
the edge all by itself anyway.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:20.970
The God Particle

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:24.920
Like its franchise predecessor, 10 Cloverfield
Lane, The Cloverfield Paradox was written

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:27.180
as an entirely separate project at first.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:32.209
Lane was based on a script called The Cellar,
while Paradox was developed as The God Particle

00:02:32.209 --> 00:02:35.580
for reasons that aren't altogether clear from
the movie itself.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:40.849
In scientific terms, a "god particle" is a
name for what is properly called a Higgs boson,

00:02:40.849 --> 00:02:44.050
a particle effectively responsible for the
origin of mass.

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:48.110
They're also theorized to have the ability
to overlap and occupy the same points in space-time

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:51.470
— unlike other particles, like electrons
or protons.

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:55.020
In theory, god particles may have played a
part in the fictional function of the Shepard

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.810
particle accelerator in earlier cuts of the
film.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:01.700
Or perhaps it just served as a cool title
to a weird sci-fi movie that dabbled in particle

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:06.600
physics, but either way, there aren't any
god particles in The Cloverfield Paradox,

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.310
so it's a good thing they changed the name.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:10.519
One world saved

00:03:10.519 --> 00:03:14.660
It's easy to chalk up the efforts of the film's
protagonists to a zero-sum game.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:18.190
They go through all of the effort to get back
to their home dimension and figure out how

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:22.430
to make the particle accelerator work, only
to realize as soon as they do that Earth is

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:25.030
now facing a problem the accelerator can't
fix.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:29.909
It's a bitter twist, but there is one silver
lining: The crew does save Earth.

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:31.849
It's just not their Earth.

00:03:31.849 --> 00:03:35.519
Right before activating the accelerator and
heading back to their Earth during the film's

00:03:35.519 --> 00:03:40.310
climax, Hamilton and Schmidt send the schematics
for the Shepard particle accelerator to the

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:43.730
parallel Earth, the one at war over energy
resources.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:48.690
It might take some time, but this planet now
has the means to access clean, renewable energy

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:53.540
and save itself … hopefully without inviting
a bunch of massive monsters into this dimension.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:54.540
Thanks for watching!

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:56.879
